{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447056-how-are-you-doing-sabbat-character-creation-in-5th-edition","id":1447056,"title":"How are you doing Sabbat character creation in 5th edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-02T16:55:39-07:00","id":1447056,"title":"How are you doing Sabbat character creation in 5th edition?","content":"I found the predator bonuses and flaws simply didn't work for Sabbat. Most paths wouldn't lose a dot of path for being an Alleycat, and most Sabbat would simply eat the Siren's spurned lover, for example. So I dropped Predator type completely. Instead, I simply gave players one more dot in their clan disciplines. I use Long Road Out of Hell's rules for tenets and convictions, and have the players create three convictions, non-human touchstones, and beast marks. I gave them seven extra background points that could only be spent on path loresheets.<br /> <br /> How do you do Sabbat character creation in 5th edition games you run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:04:25-07:00","id":1447057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447056-how-are-you-doing-sabbat-character-creation-in-5th-edition#post1447056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found the predator bonuses and flaws simply didn't work for Sabbat. Most paths wouldn't lose a dot of path for being an Alleycat, and most Sabbat would simply eat the Siren's spurned lover, for example. So I dropped Predator type completely. Instead, I simply gave players one more dot in their clan disciplines. I use Long Road Out of Hell's rules for tenets and convictions, and have the players create three convictions, non-human touchstones, and beast marks. I gave them seven extra background points that could only be spent on path loresheets.<br /> <br /> How do you do Sabbat character creation in 5th edition games you run?</div> </div> </div> </div>I homebrew that Chronicle Tenets for Sabbat are, &quot;Do not Betray the Sabbat&quot; and their Convictions are related to their Pack Members and relate the Path they follow.<br /> <br /> I also think they need their own Predator Types.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Hunter</b><br /> <br /> <b>Terrorizer</b><br /> <br /> <b>Stalker</b><br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-02-2021, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:16:39-07:00","id":1447252,"title":"","content":"Honestly it'd make sense to lose a dot of path as an alleycat. In V20 you can't start with a path rating higher than 5 (I think? That might not be true for something that uses Conscience and Self control like Honourable accord?) People are rarely good with their paths right outa character creation. <br /> <br /> Also a lot of Sabbat are really going to pick &quot;normal&quot; methods of predation when they're at home and not willing to shit on their own. The only ones that don't work are the ones that give you humanity, though honestly they'd work if they didn't give you humanity; Consensualist can be a kink, Farmer can just be convenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T18:42:47-07:00","id":1447746,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's not exactly what you're looking for, but it may help regardless. I made this lore sheet for my Mexico City chronicle, where two player characters are Sabbat defectors to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Loresheet: Sabbat Survivor </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Sabbat may be broken or gone, but you once counted yourself among their ranks. Many in your new sect, whether Camarilla or Anarchs, resent you for this, but you can also find a kind of solidarity from other Sabbat survivors - at least the ones who doesn\u2019t harbor old grudges. This loresheet represents the knowledge, secrets and potential allies you still hold on to from your Sabbat days. Because the Sabbat is such a complex sect, this lore sheet gives you two options for the second level. If you want both of those knowledges, you can choose one in lieu of a later level, just as with a Discipline. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u26ab Dark Memories </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">You knew something about what was going on in a city or region of your choice during the Sabbat days. Once per story, when you roll to discover old Sabbat secrets or acquire former Sabbat resources, you can add two dice to your pool. A twist, though, may be that the resources you\u2019re gunning for are still controlled by hidden Sabbat agents. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u26ab\u26ab Ritae</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">You\u2019ve learnt some of the </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>auctoritas ritae</i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> and the </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>ignoblis ritae</i> that the Sabbat practices. This can be used to interact with or impress Sabbat packs, but also has some real, mystical functions. You can roll Composure+Occult to perform rituals to create the following effects:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Vinculum blood bonds, where a group can pool their blood to create mutual blood bonds to each other. This makes it possible to have a group of vampires as both regnant and thrall to each other at the same time, and this group count as one individual for purposes of the Blood Potency thrall limit. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Perform a blood feast, where the blood of mortals acquire a special Blood Feast Dyscrasia. It slakes an additional Hunger, and adds two dice to all social rolls against the other vampires that partook in the blood feast . A proper blood feast will generate a lot of Stain. .</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Perform small rituals where the participants stoke the beast. This lets you regain Willpower by taking an equal number of Stain, up to the number of successes on your ritual roll. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u26ab\u26ab Rediscovered Humanity</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">You were once committed to a path of Enlightenment, the strange, inhuman philosophies of the Sabbat that let them keep the Beast at bay despite abandoning Humanity and committing horrific actions. To fit into your new sect, you elected to try and re-discover your Humanity -and succeeded against all odds. You still possess your old knowledge though, and are more detached than most. All but one of your Touchstones may be vampires, concepts, organisations or even objects instead of mortals. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab Sabbat Status </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Though you\u2019ve left the sect, you were someone in the Sabbat, you had status and deeds to your name, or you\u2019ve later acquired a good reputation and are not universally considered a traitor by the Sword of Caine. When you interact with the Sabbat, you can count with an Influence rating that\u2019s equal to your Sabbat Survivor lore rating minus one. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab Blood Brethren </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">You secretly maintain ties to the Sabbat, perhaps through old pack members or mentors that you once shared Vinculi with, perhaps through more recent acquaintances. These individuals still remain in your area, hidden away or ensconced in isolated Sabbat strongholds, and may aid you in any number of ways. You have five dots of Mawla representing your Sabbat allies. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab The Black Hand </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">You might be an undercover agent for the Sabbat, or just embroiled in some unfathomable agenda beyond your control, and are a person of interest for the Black Hand, the secretive sub-sect that serves as the elite military of the Sabbat, The shadowy, ancient leaders of the Black Hand, the Seraphim, watches you from afar, and the Hand may come to your aid in the most dire of circumstances. You can call upon the Black Hand for a major boon once per story, but their involvement tends to make things escalate <i>very</i> quickly. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T19:12:24-07:00","id":1447752,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no offense, but, I don't think I'll have much use for that loresheet. I might give the Rediscovered Humanity part to an NPC and have the players hunt him down, suck down his soul, and have his screaming soul slowly dissolve in their stomach acid. That's about it. That said, it's a well designed loresheet, just not something that would fit into my games, not as something the player characters would have, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-07-2021, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T06:00:45-07:00","id":1447802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447056-how-are-you-doing-sabbat-character-creation-in-5th-edition?p=1447746#post1447746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's not exactly what you're looking for, but i